SLLM patch 14 (phase2-cascadeexact): the shared-prefix decode attention (cascade, patches 3, 4 and 6) gives every row
bits that do not depend on the rest of the op: the other rows of the group, how many there are, the K/V view around
the row's cells. Before, two plan choices depended on the row count R = agents x G: the prefix splits (4 up to 32
rows, else 2: a different partition of the prefix and a different merge) and the prefix pass's softmax layout (8
threads x 8 cells per row with the 16-row tile, 4 x 16 with the 32-row tile: a different sum order); and auto mode
sent groups of fewer than 8 agents to ggml's kernels. So one agent's logits changed with the size of its group.
- kernels/cascade.metal: the prefix softmax uses 4 threads x C/4 cells per row with either row tile (the 16-row tile
  leaves its upper two simdgroups out of the softmax); the 32-row tile is unchanged.
- ggml-metal-cascade.{h,m}: the splits depend on the prefix length only (ggml_metal_sllm_cascade_splits, default 2,
  SLLM_CASCADE_S=N for A/Bs); auto mode takes any number of rows; a bitwise self-test at init (three shapes; one K/V
  view and 20 agents, the op over the first 1, 2, 8, 9, 17 agents must give each the bits it gets among 20); status
  fields exact_rows and splits.
- ggml-metal-cascadeq.m: the mixed-precision cascade uses the same splits rule.
- ggml-metal-qmm.{h,m}: a MUL_MAT marked op_params[13] = "SLQ1" takes qmm for a single row too (as SLLM_QMM32_N1=1
  does for every one): sllm-core marks the mat-muls of a one-row step whose row decodes through the cascade, so that
  agent computes alone what it computes in a batch. Unmarked single rows keep ggml's mat-vec (batch-1 parity).
Against llama.cpp b11669 (source tarball 620d222) after patches 0001..0011 and 0013, applied with patch -p1 in ggml/.

